Original visual material and sampled audio
------------------------------------------

The code-native chess-piece drawings, All Hallows’ Court sculpture atlases,
Celestial Observatory sculpture atlases,
launcher icons, supporting color resources, and fictional opponent identities
in the Android and iOS applications are original project material and are
covered by the Drawless Chess GPL-3.0-or-later grant. The All Hallows’ Court
atlases were generated specifically for this project with OpenAI's
image-generation tool. One image supplied by the project owner was used only as
a general gothic style, material, lighting, and quality reference; it is not
distributed with the project. The exact prompts, output hashes, and renderer
boundary are retained under artwork/all-hallows. The eight opponent portraits were generated specifically
for this project with OpenAI's image-generation tool and without third-party
reference imagery. Their full-resolution masters, final prompts, derivation
details, and hashes are retained under artwork/opponents; to the extent copyright
or related rights subsist in those outputs, they are included in the same grant.
The Celestial Observatory atlases were generated from an original project concept
without third-party reference imagery. Exact prompts, per-platform asset paths,
source dimensions, and hashes are retained under artwork/celestial-observatory;
to the extent rights subsist in the outputs, the same GPL grant applies.
Move and castling sounds are processed only from the CC0 chess contacts; captures use
the selected CC0 recording of a stone striking rocks, en passant and checkmate use the
CC0 Brick and Stone crash recordings, fireworks use the CC0 pyrotechnic recordings,
and the check cue uses a CC0 pump-action recording. Glass-crack and reserved
UI sounds also use identified MIT recordings. Android ships the processed catalog
as stereo 48 kHz Ogg/Vorbis resources; iOS ships corresponding stereo 48 kHz
AAC/M4A resources. The third-party recordings retain their original licenses;
Drawless Chess modifications and catalog code are covered by the project grant to
the extent applicable. Design and audit details are in docs/AUDIO_PROVENANCE.md.

